        522.3915405273438,
        301.5021057128906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N. Moreover, the results empirically verify the theoretical connection between the OT regularisation ε and the diffusion",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        320.7529602050781,
        541.44384765625,
        329.81890869140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "time T stated in Section 3. That is, K scales proportionally to 1 / ε in order for them to have the same level of statistical",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        332.7079772949219,
        541.4445190429688,
        341.77392578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "performance. However, as evidenced in Figure 1, the diffusion resampling is in average faster than that of OT. When both",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        344.8223571777344,
        541.43896484375,
        353.7289123535156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "methods are at their best estimation performance (i.e., ε = 0.1 and K = 32), diffusion resampling is still faster than OT.",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        356.61798095703125,
        533.7344970703125,
        365.6839294433594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "I. Linear Gaussian SSM",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        383.8479309082031,
        178.3394775390625,
        394.59564208984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Recall the model",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        404.7153625488281,
        122.95651245117188,
        413.6219177246094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Zj | Zj−1 ∼N(zj; θ1 zj−1, Id),",
      "bbox": [
        197.98300170898438,
        422.85400390625,
        326.3020324707031,
        441.6330871582031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Z0 ∼N(0, Id),",
      "bbox": [
        337.9283752441406,
        422.85400390625,
        398.9010314941406,
        441.6330871582031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Yj | Zj ∼N(yj; θ2 zj, 0.5 Id),",
      "bbox": [
        209.19798278808594,
        437.7980041503906,
        330.7460021972656,
        456.57708740234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(35)",
      "bbox": [
        525.5099487304688,
        431.3923645019531,
        542.1077270507812,
        440.2989196777344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where we set parameters θ1 = 0.5 and θ2 = 1. For each experiment, we generate a measurement sequence with j =",
      "bbox": [
        55.082000732421875,
        459.7469787597656,
        541.4465942382812,
        470.0877380371094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "0, 1, . . . , 128 steps, with N = 32 particles. The loss function estimate error ∥L−bL∥2",
      "bbox": [
        55.44000244140625,
        470.1601867675781,
        385.2520446777344,
        488.1800842285156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2 :=",
      "bbox": [
        381.2769775390625,
        471.35595703125,
        398.3678894042969,
        483.021728515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "R",
      "bbox": [
        401.1329650878906,
        470.1914978027344,
        405.8353271484375,
        476.56756591796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Θ(L(θ1, θ2)−bL(θ1, θ2))2 dθ1 dθ2,",
      "bbox": [
        405.83795166015625,
        468.0859680175781,
        542.6858520507812,
        488.1800842285156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where bL is estimated by Trapezoidal quadrature at the Cartesian grids Θ = [θ1 −0.1, θ1 + 0.1] × [θ2 −0.1, θ2 + 0.1].",
      "bbox": [
        55.082000732421875,
        485.1470031738281,
        543.1834716796875,
        503.92608642578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The filtering error is evaluated by Kullback–Leibler (KL) divergence between the true filtering distribution (which is",
      "bbox": [
        55.13100051879883,
        498.068359375,
        541.4366455078125,
        506.97491455078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a Gaussian computed exactly by a Kalman filter) and the particle filtering samples. Precisely, the error is defined by",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        510.02337646484375,
        541.7864990234375,
        518.929931640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1",
      "bbox": [
        60.606998443603516,
        519.97119140625,
        64.58206176757812,
        526.1639404296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "129",
      "bbox": [
        56.63600158691406,
        527.3291625976562,
        68.56120300292969,
        533.5219116210938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "P128",
      "bbox": [
        71.40499877929688,
        518.8841552734375,
        93.84719848632812,
        527.238525390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "j=0 KL",
      "bbox": [
        81.9219970703125,
        521.8189697265625,
        111.84452056884766,
        533.65478515625
      ],
