        526.6415405273438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N(mf",
      "bbox": [
        116.40899658203125,
        519.106201171875,
        140.38641357421875,
        530.665771484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "j , V f",
      "bbox": [
        136.5019989013672,
        519.106201171875,
        158.00439453125,
        533.4427490234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "j ) ∥N( ˆmf",
      "bbox": [
        151.90599060058594,
        519.106201171875,
        195.43939208984375,
        538.297119140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "j , ˆV f",
      "bbox": [
        191.55499267578125,
        519.106201171875,
        213.057373046875,
        533.4427490234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "j )",
      "bbox": [
        206.95896911621094,
        521.8189697265625,
        218.2134246826172,
        533.4427490234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\u0001",
      "bbox": [
        218.2119598388672,
        520.2644653320312,
        222.7748260498047,
        526.6405029296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ", where N(mf",
      "bbox": [
        222.7790069580078,
        519.106201171875,
        280.83740234375,
        530.8849487304688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "j , V f",
      "bbox": [
        276.9530029296875,
        519.106201171875,
        298.4554138183594,
        533.4427490234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "j ) is the true filtering distribution at step j, and N( ˆmf",
      "bbox": [
        292.3570251464844,
        519.106201171875,
        519.8334350585938,
        533.4427490234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "j , ˆV f",
      "bbox": [
        515.9490356445312,
        519.106201171875,
        537.451416015625,
        533.4427490234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "j )",
      "bbox": [
        531.35302734375,
        521.8189697265625,
        542.6074829101562,
        533.4427490234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "stands for the empirical approximation by the particle samples.",
      "bbox": [
        55.4400634765625,
        533.934326171875,
        306.4079284667969,
        542.8408813476562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The optimiser L-BFGS is implemented using JAXopt (Blondel et al., 2021) scipyminimize wrapper with default settings",
      "bbox": [
        55.13100051879883,
        551.8663330078125,
        541.4373168945312,
        560.7728881835938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and initial parameters θ + 1.",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        563.6619262695312,
        168.8542022705078,
        572.7279052734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We observe a numerical issue due to the gradient estimate by the resampling methods. The L-BFGS optimiser frequently",
      "bbox": [
        54.97200012207031,
        581.75439453125,
        541.7926635742188,
        590.6609497070312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "diverges. This is expected, since L-BFGS is highly sensitive to the quality of gradient estimate (Xie et al., 2020); see",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        593.7093505859375,
        541.4407348632812,
        602.6159057617188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "also Zhao & Sarmarvuori (2023) for an empirical validation. As such, when we report the results we have defined a",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        605.6653442382812,
        541.44091796875,
        614.5718994140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "convergent run by 1) positive convergence flag returned by the L-BFGS optimiser and 2) the error ∥θ −bθ∥2 < 1.9 is not",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        617.6759643554688,
        541.4425659179688,
        634.9610595703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "absurd. It turns out that the effect is especially pronounced for the soft and Gumbel-Softmax resampling, where at 100",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        630.5973510742188,
        541.4410400390625,
        639.50390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "runs, only nearly 10% return a successful flag of the optimiser, and all their estimated parameters diverge to a meaningless",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        642.5523681640625,
        541.4378662109375,
        651.4589233398438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "position. This was not problematic for the diffusion and OT samplers, where they have approximately 80% success rate in",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        654.50732421875,
        541.4373168945312,
        663.4138793945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "average.",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        666.46337890625,
        88.55567169189453,
        675.3699340820312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We also observe a numerical issue of OT implementation. By default, for instance, in OTT-JAX, gradient propagation",
      "bbox": [
        54.97200012207031,
        684.3953857421875,
        541.4403686523438,
        693.3019409179688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "through the Sinkhorn solver uses implicit differentiation by solving a linear system. This makes gradient computation of the",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        696.3513793945312,
        541.4437866210938,
        705.2579345703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "OT resampling efficient. However, the linear system often becomes ill-conditioned for most runs, and making OT parameter",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        708.3063354492188,
        541.6134033203125,
        717.212890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "20",
      "bbox": [
        293.4590148925781,
        733.2123413085938,
        303.4216003417969,
        742.118896484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    }
